<!--  
Andrea, email to Arlo, 26/2/2026: 
"I prefer to wait before sending you the draft of A since I want to be sure to have a better version of the edition. It seems that, on the basis of B as well as LOr 3963, the wrong folios have been inserted in the text (the portions “jump to …”). Version B, as well as 3963 and 15382, have preserved the correct sequence of the text.
	While the readings of B are often inferior, there are some missing clauses, etc., I also think that the text is occasionally helpful to reconstruct unclear portions of A, in the parts that overlap. Ideally, the best way to present the two texts could be a parallel arrangement as done by Willem in his editions of the prose KK. Since the text is rather badly corrupted (both versions), it is helpful to take into account every bit of evidence at our disposal (even if we decide to translate version A)."-->
