<ab type="invocation" xml:lang="san-Latn" xml:id="pamutusBuddhistA_01.01"><pb n="1v" edRef="#D"/><pb n="1r" edRef="#or3963"/><pb n="1v" edRef="#or5068"/><app><lem wit="#or3963 #or5068">namo buddhāya</lem><rdg wit="#D">aum̐ avighnām astu nāmo buddhāyā</rdg></app>!</ab>

<p n="1">pamutus saṅ <app><lem wit="#or3963 #or5068">matuha</lem><rdg cause="subtractive" wit="#D">tuha</rdg></app>, 
kayatnakəna de saṅ sevaka dharma, 
saṅ mahyun <app><lem wit="#D #or5068">maluya</lem><rdg wit="#or3963">valuya</rdg></app> viśeṣa, 
rəṅə̄n <app><lem type="norm">kojaraniṅ</lem><rdg wit="#D #or3963 #or5068">kvājaraniṅ</rdg></app> dharma, 
*amajaṅakəna pətaṅ <app><lem wit="#B">tan sakeṅ</lem><rdg wit="#D #or3963 #or5068">tasakeṅ</rdg></app> aji, 
aṅhiṅ byakta<!-- or3963 byaktaṁ --> tuhu-tuhu jugeka, 
<app><lem wit="#D #or5068">apan iṅ</lem><rdg wit="#or3963">apan ikaṅ</rdg></app> aji <app><lem wit="#D #or5068">ṅaranya</lem><rdg wit="#or3963">ṅa</rdg></app>, 
hanenucap, hana tinuduh, 
hana <app><lem wit="#D #or5068">ginə̄gvan</lem><rdg wit="#or3963">ginəgə</rdg></app>, hana inaku, maṅkana svabhāvaniṅ aji, <abbr>ṅa</abbr>.</p>

